@format 1
@id ui-event.2959244b1e3d05e8
@title Window preview key down
@section I. UI
@area UI event
@tabs Split, Edit, Convert, Audio, Merge, Funnel, Worklist, Global interface
@event-ref cs|PMainWindow/PWindow.xaml.cs|PWindow|this|PreviewKeyDown|1
@entry input
@summary Resolve configured shortcuts; the Unload gesture (F4 by default) clears the current workspace as one media-dependent state unit.
@tag preview key down
@tag PWindow
@alias owner = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace

[input] Preview key down <input>
- Receive the window preview-key event @ owner.PWindow
> editable

[editable] Did the key originate in an editor? <decision>
- Walk visual parents to protect text and password input @ owner.PWindowInputFind
? "Text input owns the key" > ignored
? "Global shortcut is allowed" > resolve

[resolve] Resolve the configured shortcut <decision>
- Format the gesture, look up its token, and dispatch it @ owner.PShortcutDispatch
? "Token is Unload" > unload
? "Another or no token" > other

[unload] Clear current workspace media <process>
- Route the Unload token through the shortcut runner and media-close handler @ owner.PShortcutRun
@ owner.PShortcutMediaClose
- Invoke the current workspace's complete media reset @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear
> output

[output] Unload handled <output>
= Preview, player, flow, sections, keyframes, waveform, files, selection, and group state are cleared together.
! Code binding: cs|PMainWindow/PWindow.xaml.cs|PWindow|this|PreviewKeyDown|1

[other] Other shortcut route <output>
= The resolved non-Unload command runs, or an unmapped gesture remains unhandled.

[ignored] Editor keeps key <output>
= No global shortcut runs.
